---
/**
 * PricingFaqBoard — graphical conversion of the pricing page FAQ.
 * 12 accordion questions grouped into 4 visual categories.
 * Uses the same .faq-item / .faq-question / .faq-answer / .faq-icon classes
 * expected by the page's existing toggle script, and preserves all copy.
 */
const groups = [
  {
    label: 'Website Rescue',
    accent: 'from-lime-400 to-lime-600',
    chip: 'bg-lime-400/15 text-lime-400',
    questions: [
      {
        q: "How do I know if my website needs a rescue or a rebuild?",
        a: `Start with the free SEO audit — it tells you whether Google can find you and flags the most obvious problems. If the issues are fixable (indexing setup, generic copy, weak structure), a rescue is usually the better investment. If the foundation itself is weak, we'll show you exactly why a rebuild makes more sense before you spend anything.`,
      },
      {
        q: "What does the $197 Rescue Report credit mean?",
        a: `The paid deep diagnostic — the <strong class="text-white">Website Rescue Report</strong> — costs <strong class="text-white">$197</strong>. If you buy it and then start setup within 60 days, the full $197 comes off your <strong class="text-white">$597 setup</strong> fee. The report is essentially risk-free: either it tells you what to fix, or it pays for itself.`,
        rich: true,
      },
      {
        q: "What does the $597 setup cover?",
        a: `One flat <strong class="text-white">$597 setup</strong> fee covers a new site or fixing the one you have. Scope is confirmed after the audit. It can cover <strong class="text-white">Found</strong> (indexing, technical SEO, Google Business Profile), <strong class="text-white">Trusted</strong> (real copy, your own photos, trust signals), <strong class="text-white">Hired</strong> (calls, forms, service pages, lead tracking) — or all three. You only pay for the setup you need.`,
        rich: true,
      },
      {
        q: "Do fix packages apply to AI-built websites?",
        a: `Yes — many of the sites we rescue were built with AI tools or templates. Common fixes include indexing setup that was never completed, robotic copy rewritten into real human copy, de-generic styling, and mobile UX repairs. The audit determines what applies to your site.`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Costs & Payments',
    accent: 'from-lime-400 to-lime-600',
    chip: 'bg-lime-400/15 text-lime-400',
    questions: [
      {
        q: "Do you offer payment plans?",
        a: `Every plan is <strong class="text-white">$597 setup</strong>, one time, followed by one monthly payment — <strong class="text-white">Core $297/month</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Plus $597/month</strong>, or <strong class="text-white">Ultra $797/month</strong>. Every plan includes hosting, SSL, backups, security, and maintenance. SEO is included — without it, the site-only Website Care Plan is <strong class="text-white">$597 setup then $149/month</strong>. Month-to-month. Cancel any time with 30 days' written notice.`,
        rich: true,
      },
      {
        q: "Is there a discount if I pay upfront?",
        a: `Yes. If you pay your <strong class="text-white">entire $597 setup plus your first monthly payment</strong> upfront in a single payment, we apply an <strong class="text-white">instant $50 discount</strong> to your total. It's the same plan and the same work — just one payment instead of two.`,
        rich: true,
      },
      {
        q: "What if I need more pages than my package includes?",
        a: `No problem! Additional pages beyond the package limit are billed at a flat rate of $75–$150 per page, depending on complexity. We can also help you prioritize which pages to launch with and add more later as your business grows.`,
      },
      {
        q: "Can I upgrade my package later?",
        a: `Absolutely. Your site is built on a scalable foundation, so upgrading is smooth. Whether you need to add e-commerce, a booking system, or more pages down the road, we can handle it. We'll simply quote the additional work based on your current package rate.`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'What You Get',
    accent: 'from-cyan-400 to-cyan-600',
    chip: 'bg-cyan-400/15 text-cyan-400',
    questions: [
      {
        q: "What's included in the price?",
        a: `Every package includes custom design, mobile responsiveness, basic SEO setup, a contact form, and hosting setup assistance.`,
      },
      {
        q: "Do you handle web hosting and domain setup?",
        a: `Yes. We'll help you choose a domain and deploy everything. Hosting, SSL, backups, security monitoring, and updates are included with every active plan — there are no separate hosting fees.`,
      },
      {
        q: "Do you offer ongoing maintenance?",
        a: `Yes — every Growth Plan is ongoing by design. Hosting, security, updates, foundational SEO, and monthly reporting are all included. See <a href="/services/seo/#growth-pricing" class="text-brand-cyan underline">full SEO pricing</a>.`,
        rich: true,
      },
      {
        q: "Do website packages include SEO?",
        a: `Yes. Foundational on-page and local SEO is included with every plan, so there is no double-charging. If you already have a site and want active local visibility work, our Plus plan at $597/month covers keyword research, content, Google Business Profile optimization, and review generation — see <a href="/services/seo/#growth-pricing" class="text-brand-cyan underline">the SEO plans</a>.`,
        rich: true,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Working With Us',
    accent: 'from-blue-400 to-blue-600',
    chip: 'bg-blue-400/15 text-blue-400',
    questions: [
      {
        q: "How long does a typical project take?",
        a: `Most projects are completed within 2–4 weeks, depending on the scope. A simple 1–2 page site can be ready in as little as 1–2 weeks, while more complex builds (e-commerce, custom portals) typically take 4–6 weeks. We'll give you a clear timeline during the proposal phase.`,
      },
      {
        q: "What if I'm not satisfied with the design?",
        a: `Your satisfaction matters. Every Growth Plan includes <strong class="text-white">one small edit request per month</strong> (up to about 30 minutes of work) plus collaborative revision rounds during the initial build. We work iteratively, sharing progress along the way so there are no surprises. Larger redesigns, new pages, and major feature work are project-priced — just ask during your consultation.`,
        rich: true,
      },
      {
        q: "What is a milestone audit?",
        a: `Every plan is audited every 90 days. If no further meaningful work is needed, we tell you — and you can pause, reduce scope, or shift to lighter maintenance. No endless retainer.`,
      },
    ],
  },
];

const icons: Record<string, string> = {
  'Website Rescue':
    'M12 2a10 10 0 100 20 10 10 0 000-20zm0 5a5 5 0 100 10 5 5 0 000-10zM7.5 7.5l9 9m0-9l-9 9',
  'Costs & Payments': 'M12 8c-1.657 0-3 .895-3 2s1.343 2 3 2 3 .895 3 2-1.343 2-3 2m0-8c1.11 0 2.08.402 2.599 1M12 8V7m0 1v8m0 0v1m0-1c-1.11 0-2.08-.402-2.599-1M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z',
  'What You Get':
    'M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z',
  'Working With Us':
    'M17 20h5v-2a4 4 0 013-3.857M9 20H4v-2a4 4 0 013-3.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z',
};
---

<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 lg:gap-5 items-start">
  {
    groups.map((group) => (
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-b from-[#3a3f49]/60 to-transparent border border-white/10 p-3.5 lg:p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4 px-1">
          <span class={`inline-flex w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-br ${group.accent} shadow-[0_0_14px_rgba(132,204,22,0.25)] items-center justify-center text-[#1c1c1c]`}>
            <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="w-5 h-5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d={icons[group.label]} />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-white font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">{group.label}</h3>
          <span class={`ml-auto text-xs font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full ${group.chip}`}>
            {group.questions.length} Q&As
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {group.questions.map((item) => (
            <div
              class="faq-item bg-[#111214] border border-white/10 rounded-xl overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 hover:border-brand-accent/30"
            >
              <button
                class="faq-question w-full flex items-center justify-between p-4 text-left transition-colors hover:bg-[#1a1b1f]"
                aria-expanded="false"
              >
                <span class="text-white font-semibold pr-3 text-sm">{item.q}</span>
                <span class="faq-icon text-brand-accent text-lg flex-shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
                <div class="px-4 pb-4 text-white/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                  {item.rich ? <Fragment set:html={item.a} /> : item.a}
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    ))
  }
</div>
